output:
```js
// tailwind.config.js
theme: { extend: { colors: { utama: "#2563eb" }, fontFamily: { sans: ["Inter"] } } }
```
`extend` adds without deleting defaults (top-level `colors` replaces everything). Then `bg-utama font-sans` work everywhere. Keep design tokens here — scattered arbitrary values (`bg-[#2563eb]`) defeat the system.

```js
// tailwind.config.js
module.exports = {
  content: ['./src/**/*.{html,js}', './*.html'],
  darkMode: 'class',
  theme: {
    extend: {
      colors: { brand: { DEFAULT: '#2563eb', light: '#93c5fd', dark: '#1e40af' } },
      fontFamily: { sans: ['Inter', 'system-ui', 'sans-serif'] },
    },
  },
  plugins: [require('@tailwindcss/forms'), require('@tailwindcss/typography')],
};
```
Content paths (missing = missing classes in prod!), class dark strategy, extended tokens (never replaced defaults), forms+typography plugins. v4 moves this into CSS `@theme`.
